  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "A model used to estimate the time it will take to hike to the top of a mountain on a trail is of the form \\(T=aL+bG,\\) where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are constants, \\(T\\) is the time in minutes, \\(L\\) is the length of the trail in miles, and \\(G\\) is the altitude gain in feet. The model estimates that it will take \\(69\\) minutes to hike to the top if a trail is \\(1.5\\) miles long and ascends \\(800\\) feet, as well as if a trail is \\(1.2\\) miles long and ascends \\(1100\\) feet.\n\nHow many minutes does the model estimate it will take to hike to the top if the trail is \\(4.2\\) miles long and ascends \\(4000\\) feet?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(240\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(246\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(252\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(258\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(264\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "246"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2024-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "From \\(1.5a+800b=1.2a+1100b\\) we get \\(0.3a=300b,\\) so \\(a=1000b.\\) Then \\(69=1.5a+800b\\) \\(=1500b+800b=2300b,\\) giving \\(b=0.03\\) and \\(a=30.\\) For \\(L=4.2,\\ G=4000,\\) \\(T=30(4.2)\\) \\(+0.03(4000)\\) \\(=126+120=246.\\) Thus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Set the two estimates equal: \\(1.5a+800b=1.2a+1100b\\)",
        "This gives \\(a=1000b,\\) so \\(69=2300b\\)"
      ],
